# Database backups — REAL CHILDREN'S RECORDS.
#
# Never committed, and worth understanding why: a git repository is copied to
# GitHub, cloned onto other machines, and keeps every version forever. One
# accidental commit of a backup would put behaviour logs and family names
# somewhere they can never be fully removed from.
backups/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# docs/ — 598 MB, and none of it belongs to this repository.
#
# It came across with the copy and is deliberately never committed. Three
# reasons, any one of which is enough:
#
#   SIZE. Git keeps every version forever. Half a gigabyte in the history is
#   half a gigabyte in every clone, for all four of us, for good.
#
#   LICENCE. Much of it is Mobbin's licensed captures of Customer.io's product
#   and Figma exports. Redistributing those in a public repository is not ours
#   to do. They are reference material, not an asset of this project.
#
#   RELEVANCE. The planning documents describe the original build and the work
#   still outstanding on it. That is a different project with a different team.
#
# The files stay on disk so they can still be read while porting a screen over.
# They simply never enter git. Delete the folder from THIS repo whenever you
# want the disk space back — the originals live in the other one.
docs/
